# What goes into the api image, as an allowlist.
#
# ⚠️ **Everything is excluded and then re-included by name, on purpose.** This
# was a denylist, and a denylist means every file added later is baked into the
# image by default — so `SEC_AUDIT.md`, `PROJECT_STATE.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and
# `docs/REMOTE_SERVER.md` all shipped inside the container on every box. Repo
# visibility does nothing about that: the image is built on the box from the
# clone. An allowlist inverts the default, so a new document stays out until
# someone decides otherwise.
#
# ⚠️ Derived from the Dockerfile and the entrypoint, not guessed:
#
#   * `ENTRYPOINT ["/app/docker/entrypoint.sh"]`, and the build does
#     `chmod +x` on it — excluding `docker/` fails the build outright.
#   * the entrypoint runs `alembic upgrade head`, so `alembic/` and
#     `alembic.ini` have to be here.
#   * `app/version.py` reads `VERSION` at run time.
#   * `dist/` is **not** needed: the seeder reads `${TAKMDM_SEED_DIR:-/seed}`,
#     which compose bind-mounts from `./dist`. Keeping it out of the image saves
#     28 MB of the 38 MB context and changes nothing, because nothing ever read
#     `/app/dist`.
#   * `pki/` is a bind mount and must never be baked in.
#
# `tests/`, `agent/`, `scripts/`, `docs/`, `.github/` and the working documents
# are all absent from the image now. None of them is read at run time — every
# reference to `tests/` in `app/` is prose in a comment.

*

# The application itself.
!app
!alembic
!alembic.ini
!VERSION

# The entrypoint, which is also the image's ENTRYPOINT. The nginx and systemd
# files beside it are host-side, and cost 36 KB to carry rather than split.
!docker

# Installed in an earlier layer, and kept so a rebuild inside the image is
# possible without the repository.
!requirements.txt

# Apache 2.0 §4: a distribution that carries the work carries these. A container
# image is a distribution, and 13 KB is not worth the argument.
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# ⚠️ Re-excluded *after* the re-includes above, because `!app` pulls in
# everything beneath it. Caches and virtualenvs inside the tree would otherwise
# ride along.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
